{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a17b2c-9a00-72cc-926e-ce24bc16620b","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/home/user/app/context/phase1/spec/ShiftProof-interface.md","limit":2000},"result":"... (truncated)\ncontract against §5 and §10 without the author’s context.\\n   375\\t\\n   376\\t### 10.2 What “secure” does not mean here\\n   377\\t\\n   378\\t\\n   379\\t### 14.2 Unit test cases\\n   380\\t\\n   381\\t| ID | Test | Expected |\\n   382\\t|---|---|---|\\n   383\\t| U01 | Create with valid worker/rate/duration | `ShiftCreated`; escrow pulled; `nextShiftId` increments |\\n   384\\t| U02 | Create with zero worker | `ZeroAddress`/`InvalidWorker` |\\n   385\\t| U03 | Create with worker == employer | `InvalidWorker` |\\n   386\\t| U04 | Create with zero rate | `InvalidAmount` |\\n   387\\t| U05 | Create with zero duration | `InvalidDuration` |\\n   388\\t| U06 | Create with duration > 24h | `DurationTooLong` |\\n   389\\t| U07 | Create with escrow > 10,000 USDC | `EscrowTooLarge` |\\n   390\\t| U08 | Create with insufficient allowance/balance | USDC revert; no shift |\\n   391\\t| U09 | Create with a 6-decimal mock | Works |\\n   392\\t| U10 | Create with an 18-decimal token | `InvalidDecimals` |\\n   393\\t| U11 | Clock in by worker | `Active`; `startedAt` set |\\n   394\\t| U12 | Clock in by non-worker | `NotWorker` |\\n   395\\t| U13 | Clock in twice | `InvalidStatus` |\\n   396\\t| U14 | Clock out by worker | `AwaitingAttestation`; `endedAt` set |\\n   397\\t| U15 | Clock out before clock-in | `InvalidStatus` |\\n   398\\t| U16 | Clock in and out in the same block | Allowed; `endedAt == startedAt` |\\n   399\\t| U17 | Attest by employer | `Attested`; `owed` correct; no USDC movement |\\n   400\\t| U18 | Attest by non-employer | `NotEmployer` |\\n   401\\t| U19 | Attest seconds > max | `AttestedTooLong` |\\n   402\\t| U20 | Attest 0 | `Attested`; `owed = 0` |\\n   403\\t| U21 | Attest full | `owed = escrow` |\\n   404\\t| U22 | Attest from `Funded` (timer skip) | `Attested`; `endedAt` set |\\n   405\\t| U23 | Attest from `Active` | `Attested`; `endedAt` set |\\n   406\\t| U24 | Claim by worker | USDC to worker; `Claimed`/`Settled` |\\n   407\\t| U25 | Claim by non-worker | `NotWorker` |\\n   408\\t| U26 | Claim twice | `InvalidStatus` |\\n   409\\t| U27 | Claim with zero owed | `NothingToClaim` |\\n   410\\t| U28 | Refund unused by anyone | USDC to employer; escrow reduced |\\n   411\\t| U29 | Refund before attest | `InvalidStatus` |\\n   412\\t| U30 | Refund twice | `NothingToRefund` |\\n   413\\t| U31 | Refund after claim | Residual to employer; `Settled` |\\n   414\\t| U32 | Cancel by employer in `Funded` | Full refund; `Cancelled` |\\n   415\\t| U33 | Cancel by non-employer | `NotEmployer` |\\n   416\\t| U34 | Cancel after clock-in | `InvalidStatus` |\\n   417\\t| U35 | Cancel twice | `InvalidStatus` |\\n   418\\t| U36 | Read nonexistent shift | `None`/zero fields |\\n   419\\t| U37 | `getShifts` with >50 IDs | `TooManyIds` |\\n   420\\t| U38 | Direct USDC donation | Balance increases; `totalEscrow` unchanged; no sweep |\\n   421\\t| U39 | Reentrant mock token | `nonReentrant` blocks; no double spend |\\n   422\\t| U40 | Event arguments/indexing | Match ABI |\\n   423\\t\\n   424\\t### 14.3 Fuzz and invariant tests\\n   425\\t\\n   426\\t**Fuzz:**\\n   427\\t\\n   428\\t- `hourlyRate` uniform in `[1, 1_000e6]`.\\n   429\\t- `maxSeconds` uniform in `[1, 86_400]`.\\n   430\\t- `attestedSeconds` uniform in `[0, maxSeconds]`.\\n   431\\t- Random actor for each call; expected revert only for documented guards.\\n   432\\t- Assert `owed <= escrow`, `escrow <= maxEscrow`, `totalEscrow` reflects the sum.\\n   433\\t\\n   434\\t**Invariant handler:**\\n   435\\t\\n   436\\t- `create`, `clockIn`, `clockOut`, `attest`, `claim`, `refundUnused`, `cancel` with bounded random inputs and actors.\\n   437\\t- After each sequence: contract balance ≥ `totalEscrow`; no shift’s escrow increased; no double claim; terminal states reject writes; `totalEscrow` equals the sum.\\n   438\\t- Seed with a few hand-written sequences to ensure coverage.\\n   439\\t\\n   440\\t### 14.4 Fork and integration tests\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_01L2kXWdLidVMPekjzZCgFFU\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.18\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}"}}
{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a17b2c-9a01-755a-9ffb-84fc9a5fa5d4","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/home/user/app/contracts/ShiftProof.sol","limit":2000},"result":"... (truncated)\n4\\t\\n   245\\t        if (s.escrow == 0) {\\n   246\\t            s.status = Status.Settled;\\n   247\\t        } else {\\n   248\\t            s.status = Status.Claimed;\\n   249\\t        }\\n   250\\t\\n   251\\t        // --- Interactions ---\\n   252\\t        IERC20(usdc).safeTransfer(s.worker, amount);\\n   253\\t\\n   254\\t        emit Claimed(shiftId, s.worker, amount);\\n   255\\t        if (s.status == Status.Settled) {\\n   256\\t            emit Settled(shiftId);\\n   257\\t        }\\n   258\\t    }\\n   259\\t\\n   260\\t    /// @notice Permissionless: return escrow in excess of owed back to the employer.\\n   261\\t    ///         Accepts Attested (before claim) or Claimed (after claim); always pays employer.\\n   262\\t    function refundUnused(uint256 shiftId) external nonReentrant {\\n   263\\t        Shift storage s = _shifts[shiftId];\\n   264\\t        if (s.status == Status.None) revert InvalidStatus();\\n   265\\t        if (s.status != Status.Attested && s.status != Status.Claimed) revert InvalidStatus();\\n   266\\t        if (s.escrow <= s.owed) revert NothingToRefund();\\n   267\\t\\n   268\\t        // --- Effects ---\\n   269\\t        uint256 amount = s.escrow - s.owed;\\n   270\\t        s.escrow = s.owed;\\n   271\\t        totalEscrow -= amount;\\n   272\\t\\n   273\\t        // Settle when escrow drops to zero and the worker has already been paid (or owed == 0).\\n   274\\t        bool terminal = (s.escrow == 0 && (s.status == Status.Claimed || s.owed == 0));\\n   275\\t        if (terminal) {\\n   276\\t            s.status = Status.Settled;\\n   277\\t        }\\n   278\\t\\n   279\\t        address employer = s.employer;\\n   280\\t\\n   281\\t        // --- Interactions ---\\n   282\\t        IERC20(usdc).safeTransfer(employer, amount);\\n   283\\t\\n   284\\t        emit UnusedRefunded(shiftId, employer, amount);\\n   285\\t        if (terminal) {\\n   286\\t            emit Settled(shiftId);\\n   287\\t        }\\n   288\\t    }\\n   289\\t\\n   290\\t    /// @notice Employer cancels a shift that has never been clocked in; full refund.\\n   291\\t    function cancel(uint256 shiftId) external nonReentrant {\\n   292\\t        Shift storage s = _shifts[shiftId];\\n   293\\t        if (s.status == Status.None) revert InvalidStatus();\\n   294\\t        if (msg.sender != s.employer) revert NotEmployer();\\n   295\\t        if (s.status != Status.Funded) revert InvalidStatus();\\n   296\\t\\n   297\\t        // --- Effects ---\\n   298\\t        uint256 amount = s.escrow;\\n   299\\t        s.escrow    = 0;\\n   300\\t        totalEscrow -= amount;\\n   301\\t        s.status    = Status.Cancelled;\\n   302\\t\\n   303\\t        address employer = s.employer;\\n   304\\t\\n   305\\t        // --- Interactions ---\\n   306\\t        IERC20(usdc).safeTransfer(employer, amount);\\n   307\\t\\n   308\\t        emit Cancelled(shiftId, employer, amount);\\n   309\\t    }\\n   310\\t\\n   311\\t    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n   312\\t    // View functions\\n   313\\t    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n   314\\t\\n   315\\t    /// @notice Return a single shift. Unknown IDs return a zero-valued struct with status None.\\n   316\\t    function getShift(uint256 shiftId) external view returns (Shift memory) {\\n   317\\t        return _shifts[shiftId];\\n   318\\t    }\\n   319\\t\\n   320\\t    /// @notice Return multiple shifts. At most 50 IDs per call.\\n   321\\t    function getShifts(uint256[] calldata shiftIds) external view returns (Shift[] memory) {\\n   322\\t        if (shiftIds.length > 50) revert TooManyIds();\\n   323\\t        Shift[] memory result = new Shift[](shiftIds.length);\\n   324\\t        for (uint256 i = 0; i < shiftIds.length; i++) {\\n   325\\t            result[i] = _shifts[shiftIds[i]];\\n   326\\t        }\\n   327\\t        return result;\\n   328\\t    }\\n   329\\t}\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_01NqxDB9qCyb142MPnRiUZfx\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.18\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}"}}
{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a17b2c-99ff-7179-bac4-27a47c9151d1","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/home/user/app/contracts/test/ShiftProof.t.sol","limit":2000},"result":"... (truncated)\nuint256 idSeed) external {\\n  1011\\t        if (createdIds.length == 0) return;\\n  1012\\t        uint256 id = createdIds[idSeed % createdIds.length];\\n  1013\\t        vm.prank(actors[2]);\\n  1014\\t        try sp.refundUnused(id) {} catch {}\\n  1015\\t    }\\n  1016\\t\\n  1017\\t    function cancel(uint256 idSeed) external {\\n  1018\\t        if (createdIds.length == 0) return;\\n  1019\\t        uint256 id = createdIds[idSeed % createdIds.length];\\n  1020\\t        vm.prank(actors[0]);\\n  1021\\t        try sp.cancel(id) {} catch {}\\n  1022\\t    }\\n  1023\\t\\n  1024\\t    function getCreatedIds() external view returns (uint256[] memory) {\\n  1025\\t        return createdIds;\\n  1026\\t    }\\n  1027\\t}\\n  1028\\t\\n  1029\\tcontract InvariantTest is Test {\\n  1030\\t    ShiftProof        internal sp;\\n  1031\\t    MockUSDC          internal usdc;\\n  1032\\t    ShiftProofHandler internal handler;\\n  1033\\t\\n  1034\\t    function setUp() public {\\n  1035\\t        usdc    = new MockUSDC(6);\\n  1036\\t        sp      = new ShiftProof(address(usdc));\\n  1037\\t        handler = new ShiftProofHandler(sp, usdc);\\n  1038\\t\\n  1039\\t        targetContract(address(handler));\\n  1040\\t    }\\n  1041\\t\\n  1042\\t    /// INV-01: contract USDC balance >= totalEscrow\\n  1043\\t    function invariant_solvency() public view {\\n  1044\\t        assertGe(usdc.balanceOf(address(sp)), sp.totalEscrow());\\n  1045\\t    }\\n  1046\\t\\n  1047\\t    /// INV-02: totalEscrow equals sum of per-shift escrow\\n  1048\\t    function invariant_totalEscrow_sum() public view {\\n  1049\\t        uint256[] memory ids = handler.getCreatedIds();\\n  1050\\t        uint256 sum;\\n  1051\\t        for (uint i = 0; i < ids.length; i++) {\\n  1052\\t            sum += sp.getShift(ids[i]).escrow;\\n  1053\\t        }\\n  1054\\t        assertEq(sp.totalEscrow(), sum);\\n  1055\\t    }\\n  1056\\t\\n  1057\\t    /// INV-03: owed <= escrow for every shift\\n  1058\\t    function invariant_owed_le_escrow() public view {\\n  1059\\t        uint256[] memory ids = handler.getCreatedIds();\\n  1060\\t        for (uint i = 0; i < ids.length; i++) {\\n  1061\\t            ShiftProof.Shift memory s = sp.getShift(ids[i]);\\n  1062\\t            assertLe(s.owed, s.escrow);\\n  1063\\t        }\\n  1064\\t    }\\n  1065\\t\\n  1066\\t    /// INV-04: Claimed implies owed == 0\\n  1067\\t    function invariant_claimed_owed_zero() public view {\\n  1068\\t        uint256[] memory ids = handler.getCreatedIds();\\n  1069\\t        for (uint i = 0; i < ids.length; i++) {\\n  1070\\t            ShiftProof.Shift memory s = sp.getShift(ids[i]);\\n  1071\\t            if (s.status == ShiftProof.Status.Claimed) {\\n  1072\\t                assertEq(s.owed, 0);\\n  1073\\t            }\\n  1074\\t        }\\n  1075\\t    }\\n  1076\\t\\n  1077\\t    /// INV: Settled implies escrow == 0 and owed == 0\\n  1078\\t    function invariant_settled_zero() public view {\\n  1079\\t        uint256[] memory ids = handler.getCreatedIds();\\n  1080\\t        for (uint i = 0; i < ids.length; i++) {\\n  1081\\t            ShiftProof.Shift memory s = sp.getShift(ids[i]);\\n  1082\\t            if (s.status == ShiftProof.Status.Settled) {\\n  1083\\t                assertEq(s.escrow, 0);\\n  1084\\t                assertEq(s.owed, 0);\\n  1085\\t            }\\n  1086\\t        }\\n  1087\\t    }\\n  1088\\t\\n  1089\\t    /// INV: Cancelled implies escrow == 0 and owed == 0\\n  1090\\t    function invariant_cancelled_zero() public view {\\n  1091\\t        uint256[] memory ids = handler.getCreatedIds();\\n  1092\\t        for (uint i = 0; i < ids.length; i++) {\\n  1093\\t            ShiftProof.Shift memory s = sp.getShift(ids[i]);\\n  1094\\t            if (s.status == ShiftProof.Status.Cancelled) {\\n  1095\\t                assertEq(s.escrow, 0);\\n  1096\\t                assertEq(s.owed, 0);\\n  1097\\t            }\\n  1098\\t        }\\n  1099\\t    }\\n  1100\\t}\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_01FPm21hux6YD71Mb55aCfst\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.18\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}"}}
