{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"sandbox_step","step":"file_written","status":"running","path":"/home/user/app/AGENTS.md","toolCallId":"01a17b31-5f78-7127-a42f-b706c35e56e0"}}
{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"file_write_streaming","toolCallId":"01a17b31-5f78-7127-a42f-b706c35e56e0","path":"/home/user/app/AGENTS.md","status":"running","chunk":"# ShiftProof\n\n> Built with Arc Studio - money-powered apps in minutes\n\nThis is the **project memory** - what Arc Studio remembers about building this app. It helps future agents (or humans) understand and extend the project.\n\n---\n\n## What This App Does\n\nShiftProof is a per-shift USDC escrow contract with optional clock-in/out and employer attestation. Employers fund a shift, workers clock in/out, employers attest hours, workers claim pay, and unused escrow is refunded permissionlessly. No admin, owner, pause, upgrade, fee, or sweep functions.\n\n## Contract Status\n\n- `contracts/ShiftProof.sol` — deployed: not yet (testnet deploy pending).\n- `contracts/test/ShiftProof.t.sol` — **76/76 tests passing** (unit, reentrancy, read, fuzz, invariant). Last run: 2026-10-27.\n- `contracts/test/MockUSDC.sol` — test-only; includes `ReentrantMockToken`.\n- `contracts/script/Deploy.s.sol` — deployment script; asserts chain ID and USDC address before broadcast.\n\n## Test Fix Notes (2026-10-27)\n\nTwo tests in `CreateShiftTest` were failing due to `vm.prank` consumption by cheatcode/external calls:\n\n- `test_create_max_rate_boundary`: `sp.MAX_HOURLY_RATE()` (external call) consumed the preceding prank before `createShift`. Fixed by reading the constant into a local variable before `vm.prank`.\n- `test_create_rate_above_max_reverts`: `vm.expectRevert` (cheatcode call) consumed the prank. Fixed by placing `vm.expectRevert` before `vm.prank`.\n\nNo contract changes were made; the spec was not violated.","oldContent":"# [App Name]\n\n> Built with Arc Studio - money-powered apps in minutes\n\nThis is the **project memory** - what Arc Studio remembers about building this app. It helps future agents (or humans) understand and extend the project.\n\n---\n\n## What This App Does\n\n[Brief description of what the app does and its primary use case]","totalLines":27,"oldTotalLines":11}}
{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a17b31-5f78-7127-a42f-b706c35e56e0","toolName":"edit_file","args":{"file_path":"/home/user/app/AGENTS.md","old_string":"[redacted]","new_string":"[redacted]"},"result":"Successfully replaced 1 occurrence(s) in '/home/user/app/AGENTS.md'\n\nResulting context around the edit:\n 1\t# ShiftProof\n 2\t\n 3\t> Built with Arc Studio - money-powered apps in minutes\n 4\t\n 5\tThis is the **project memory** - what Arc Studio remembers about building this app. It helps future agents (or humans) understand and extend the project.\n 6\t\n 7\t---\n 8\t\n 9\t## What This App Does\n10\t\n... (7 lines not shown) ...\n18\t- `contracts/script/Deploy.s.sol` — deployment script; asserts chain ID and USDC address before broadcast.\n19\t\n20\t## Test Fix Notes (2026-10-27)\n21\t\n22\tTwo tests in `CreateShiftTest` were failing due to `vm.prank` consumption by cheatcode/external calls:\n23\t\n24\t- `test_create_max_rate_boundary`: `sp.MAX_HOURLY_RATE()` (external call) consumed the preceding prank before `createShift`. Fixed by reading the constant into a local variable before `vm.prank`.\n25\t- `test_create_rate_above_max_reverts`: `vm.expectRevert` (cheatcode call) consumed the prank. Fixed by placing `vm.expectRevert` before `vm.prank`.\n26\t\n27\tNo contract changes were made; the spec was not violated.\n28\t\n29\t## Tech Stack\n30\t"}}
